all the red shells and mushrooms in the  world wouldn't help a driver who still  has their training license so feel proud  when you wave that checkered flag those  days when Mario Kart used to serve up  first place on a silver platter have  gone the way of the Virtual Boy  now it takes raw skill and stubborn  determination to rise above the madness  and the experience couldn't be better  for it  I earned every one of my victories in  Mario Kart 8 and took great pleasure and  wiping that foolish smile off Donkey  Kong's face turns in Mario Kart 8  backing you to power slide ramps purrs  you to boost off them and performing  tight maneuvers through the many snaking  twists is a difficult endeavor that's  immensely rewarding the feeling of the  ground beneath your tires or hover pads  when you ride up walls and ceilings it's  so tight and immediately you're one with  the road your prize for braving the  challenges loneliness you can stay  safely in first place once you've  mastered the racing lines let everyone  else battle for second  you see those dastardly items that have  been the scourge of my existence in  previous mario karts have had their  impact drastically reduced  oh there are still blue shells that  punish those with talents and lightning  bolts that place a shrinking handicap on  the entire field but their effects  aren't nearly as great as recent entries  if you're smart behind the wheel a mere  shell is little more than a speed bump  so don't be discouraged when you're  struck skill being more important than  items is true rather than you're racing  against the computer or a group of your  friends sure there are times when you're  struck by a couple items at quick  succession but such moments of  profession are rare enough that you  always feel in control  this emphasis on racing ability means  that it's harder to come back once you  fall behind if you find yourself in the  middle of a pack there are so many items  about that your rhythm is constantly  interrupted and there aren't any instant  win items either it takes a lot of  effort to claw yourself back to the top  so my advice is to not fall behind in  the first place Mario karts racing is as  good as the franchise has seen and not  just because you're driving sales are so  much more important than item lock it's  the feeling of rounding corners it's so  diller a ting of gliding through the air  and deftly skirting hazards littering  the ground earning boosts through turns  requires steely concentration the longer  you hold your drift  the faster you shoot out of the turn  it's a tense game of chicken pushing  your rider to his/her or its limit as  great as the racing is in Mario Kart 8  there are a couple head-scratching  features that stand out like sore thumbs  why for instance isn't there clock and  Grand Prix do we really need so many  different kart parts who thought it was  a good idea for the default option after  a race to be view highlight reel oh and  of the 30 playable characters there are  two palace swaps five babies and seven  Koopa kids very boring one last  complaint and this is a biggie  battle mode is pretty terrible instead  of specially-made arenas you choose from  eight of the racing tracks driving  aimlessly around trying to find your  friends is the exact opposite of fun  sure the whole battle mode thing became  past day a few years back but having  everyone fight on racetracks doesn't fix  that all right enough poking holes in  this ridiculous game Mario Kart 8 is an  achievement because it's still as warm  and welcoming as you'd expect but isn't  so desperate to be like that it waters  down the experience for those who don't  need a helping hand and the tracks  demand precise driving with shortcuts  that only the most daring will  consistently reach there are some duds  out there such as toads Turnpike from  Mario Kart 64 but most of the 32 are  worth putting serious time into until  you master their  many turns nintendo has done a fine job  of keeping mario kart relevant how many  franchises have remained in peak form  for more than 20 years  not many I admit that in the early going  yawns it's more mario karts but as I  rose through the ranks and learn the  courses my tone shifted one of  excitements it's more mario karts and  i'm happy nintendo hasn't forgotten what  makes this series so darn fun  Oh
 

